{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_delta","contentIndex":0,"delta":"Test List Phase Complete","partial":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Test List\n\nTest List Created:\n**Feature**: MHPCO Claim Office Policy Management\n**Test File**: src/claim-office.spec.ts\n**Tests**: 42\n\n**Test Cases** (ordered simple -> complex):\n1. should calculate empty item list premium as 5 G -- only processing fee\n2. should calculate sword base premium as 100 G\n3. should calculate amulet base premium as 60 G\n4. should calculate staff base premium as 80 G\n5. should calculate potion base premium as 40 G\n6. should calculate component (rune/moonstone) base premium as 25 G each\n7. should apply special 60 G premium for exactly 3 alike components\n8. should not apply block discount to 4 or more components of the same type\n9. should not apply block discount across different component types\n10. should apply multiple blocks for multiple sets of 3 alike components\n11. should add 50% surcharge to cursed items\n12. should add 30% surcharge to highly enchanted items (enchantment ≥ 5)\n13. should apply cursed surcharge only to the base premium of the cursed item in multi-item policies\n14. should apply high enchantment surcharge only to the base premium of the enchanted item in multi-item policies\n15. should apply both cursed and high enchantment surcharges when both conditions are met\n16. should apply 20% loyalty discount for customers with ≥ 2 years with MHPCO\n17. should apply 10% initial assessment surcharge for first insurance\n18. should apply 15% follow-up contract discount for contracts after the first\n19. should apply processing fee of 5 G to every premium\n20. should apply first insurance surcharge to new items even for long-standing customers\n21. should calculate premium as 165 G for newcomer with cursed sword\n22. should calculate premium as 160 G for long-standing customer's second contract with cursed, highly enchanted sword\n23. should round final premium up to whole G in MHPCO's favor when fractional\n24. should keep intermediate calculations as fractions, only rounding final result\n25. should apply 100 G deductible per damage event\n26. should cap total payout per policy at twice the insurance sum\n27. should reimburse damage to items with enchantment ≥ 8 at 50% of damage amount\n28. should fully reimburse damage to items made of dragon material\n29. should apply both dragon material and high enchantment rules when both conditions are met, with 50% rule taking precedence\n30. should fully reimburse dragon material items with enchantment < 8\n31. should apply only high enchantment rule (50%) to non-dragon material items with enchantment ≥ 8\n32. should apply deductible separately to each damaged item in multi-item damage events\n33. should support multiple items of the same type in a policy\n34. should reject claim when damages include more items of a type than are insured\n35. should reduce payout when remaining cap is less than calculated payout\n36. should update remaining cap after each claim\n37. should set remaining cap to zero when fully exhausted\n38. should calculate insurance sum as sum of items' insurance values, regardless of component block discounts\n39. should set cap as twice the insurance sum based on unmodified insurance values\n40. should exit with error for quote with unknown item type\n41. should exit with error for claim referencing item not part of policy\n42. should exit with error for claim with negative damage amount\n43. should exit with error for claim with unknown item type in damages\n\nTest List Phase Complete"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784971513180,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-316557ed-42bb-4fea-95f5-09